  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "M2 finalized transport",
      "conclusion": "New opt-ins remain separate from native finalized fields. Exact immutable RPM, metadata absence or explicit native carry, current master and ACTIVE tuple checks run before proof publication. Issued replay compares the recomputed sealed proof; no generic curriculum or course inference added by this merge."
    },
    {
      "area": "M2 problem renderer",
      "conclusion": "New main helper stays limited to its exact three UID/source/ordinal bindings and one exclusive authority lane. Immutable native, prefigure/current sources and full assets, original independent observation plus six-case student UI evidence are checked before four in-memory display fields are restored and the original reassessment validator is called. Current payload digest and original proof digest remain sealed."
    },
    {
      "area": "AutoMeta and durable sidecars",
      "conclusion": "New old-cursor path requires complete native source-review revalidation and exact whole-question digest from the bound original/prefigure snapshots. Existing old M2 renderer, provider renderer, recovery, RPM ordinary/solution leaf and alias modules are preserved. The new sidecar option is appended without deleting old options."
    },
    {
      "area": "Scope and four-slot preservation",
      "conclusion": "Fixed scope guard, private checked-full-pass cache-rekey capability, PR capture/finalassert and full four-slot pass stay byte-identical to ours. Main only extends the writer four-slot input fingerprint with existing-vector carrier directory; it does not authorize semantic changes or bypass full checks."
    },
    {
      "area": "Main race",
      "conclusion": "Default remains three attempts; explicit CLI budget caps at six. Only origin/main can opt in to the fixed all-heads refspec. Evidence hydration excludes main after capturing the retry base, does not checkout or merge the evidence branch, and preserves ordinary regeneration/reapply checks, candidate verification, failed-digest refusal and nonforce push."
    }
  ],
